Clarifying Questions

"Before designing, let me clarify a few things."

Is the cart per-session or persistent across logins?
Can the same product appear multiple times, or just update quantity?
What discount types — percentage, flat, category-specific, BOGO?
Do we need cart item add-ons like gift wrap, extended warranty?
Do we need order cancellation and returns?
What happens if stock runs out between add-to-cart and checkout?


Assumptions:

Cart is persistent, tied to a user account
Same product → update quantity, not duplicate line items
Discounts via coupon codes: PERCENTAGE, FLAT, CATEGORY-BASED
Cart item add-ons via Decorator pattern
Inventory reserved at checkout, released if payment fails
Order cancellation supported (before SHIPPED)


1. Functional & Non-Functional Requirements

Functional

Browse and search products by category
Add / remove / update quantity in cart
Apply add-ons to cart items (gift wrap, warranty)
Apply coupon code at checkout
Checkout → inventory reservation → payment → order confirmed
View order history and track order status
Cancel order (before shipped), return order (after delivered)


Non-Functional

No overselling: two users buying the last unit simultaneously — exactly one succeeds
Price lock: product price captured at checkout time, not at add-to-cart time
Undo support: user can undo the last cart operation
Extensibility: new add-on types, discount types, order states addable without touching existing logic


2. Core Entities
Product          → catalog item with stock (AtomicInteger for thread safety)
Cart             → user's active basket, holds CartItemComponents
CartItemComponent→ interface — Decorator pattern root
BaseCartItem     → concrete component (product + quantity)
GiftWrapDecorator        → wraps CartItemComponent, adds ₹50
ExtendedWarrantyDecorator→ wraps CartItemComponent, adds ₹500
Coupon           → discount code with type, value, validity
Order            → snapshot of cart at checkout (immutable after placed)
OrderItem        → snapshot of one line item (price locked at checkout)
Payment          → linked to an order
Address          → record (Java 21)


3. API Design
Method	   Endpoint	                                         Purpose
---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET	       /api/v1/products?category=&q=	                Browse/search
GET	       /api/v1/cart/{userId}	                        View cart
POST       /api/v1/cart/{userId}/items	                    Add item (+ add-ons)
PUT	       /api/v1/cart/{userId}/items/{productId}	        Update quantity
DELETE     /api/v1/cart/{userId}/items/{productId}	        Remove item
DELETE     /api/v1/cart/{userId}/undo	                    Undo last operation
POST       /api/v1/cart/{userId}/checkout	                {couponCode, paymentMode, address} → Order
GET	       /api/v1/orders/{userId}	                        Order history
PUT	       /api/v1/orders/{orderId}/cancel	                Cancel order


4. Design Patterns — what, where, why
Pattern         	Where	                                   What's new
===============================================================================================
Decorator	  CartItemComponent hierarchy	       ✅ NEW — stack add-ons (gift wrap + warranty) without a boolean explosion on CartItem
Command	      CartCommand + CartCommandInvoker	   ✅ NEW — every cart mutation is an undoable command object; history stack enables undo
Facade	      CheckoutService	                   ✅ NEW — hides 6-step checkout orchestration (validate → reserve → discount → order → pay → notify) behind one method
Strategy	  DiscountStrategy	                   Same pattern, different axis — coupon-based discount calculation
State	      OrderState	                       Same pattern as Booking in hotel — PLACED → CONFIRMED → SHIPPED → DELIVERED → CANCELLED
Observer	  OrderObserver	                       Same — email + SMS on order placed/shipped/delivered
Builder       Order	                               Snapshot has many fields — required (items, total, address) and optional (coupon, notes)
Factory       DiscountStrategyFactory	           Exhaustive switch on CouponType — same as all previous systems
Singleton	  ShoppingApp	                       One product catalog + order ledger
Repository	  All four repos	                   Same — interface over ConcurrentHashMap


